/*! @brief File object is used to represent files in the file system, compatible with Web standard File API.

File inherits from Blob, in addition to having all Blob's binary data capabilities, it also adds properties such as filename (name) and last modified time (lastModified), commonly used in scenarios such as file upload, download, Web API interaction, etc.

Main features:
1. Inherits from Blob, supports all binary data operations, slicing, asynchronous reading, etc.
2. Read-only property name: represents the filename, usually used for display, upload or saving files.
3. Read-only property lastModified: represents the file's last modified time (milliseconds since 1970-01-01 00:00:00 UTC).
4. Constructor requires filename parameter to be passed, otherwise throws TypeError.
5. Can specify type, endings, lastModified and other options during construction, behavior is consistent with Web File API.

Common usage example:
```JavaScript
// Create File object
const file = new File(["hello"], "greeting.txt", { type: "text/plain" });

// Read filename and type
console.log(file.name); // "greeting.txt"
console.log(file.type); // "text/plain"

// Get last modified time
console.log(file.lastModified);

// Slice
const part = file.slice(0, 2);

// Asynchronous read content
file.text().then(txt => console.log(txt));
```
*/
interface File : Blob
{
    /*!@brief File constructor, creates a new File instance. File inherits from Blob, supports all Blob data types.

    options supports the following properties:
       - type: specifies MIME type (such as "text/plain"), defaults to empty string.
       - lastModified: specifies last modified time (timestamp in milliseconds), defaults to current time.
    
     @param blobParts Initialization data array, can contain strings, ArrayBuffer, TypedArray, Blob, etc.
     @param name Filename, must be a string, represents the name of the file (such as "a.txt"), cannot be empty.
     @param options Optional parameter object
    */
    File(Array blobParts, String name, Object options = {});

    /*!@brief File constructor, creates a new File instance. File inherits from Blob, supports all Blob data types.

    options supports the following properties:
       - type: specifies MIME type (such as "text/plain"), defaults to empty string.
       - lastModified: specifies last modified time (timestamp in milliseconds), defaults to current time.
    
     @param blobData Initialized binary data, can be Buffer or other binary data types.
     @param name Filename, must be a string, represents the name of the file (such as "a.txt"), cannot be empty.
     @param options Optional parameter object
    */
    File(Buffer blobData, String name, Object options = {});

    /*!@brief File constructor, creates a new File instance. File inherits from Blob, supports all Blob data types.

    options supports the following properties:
       - data: initialized binary data, can be Buffer or other binary data types.
       - name: filename, must be a string, represents the name of the file (such as "a.txt"), cannot be empty.
       - type: specifies MIME type (such as "text/plain"), defaults to empty string.
       - lastModified: specifies last modified time (timestamp in milliseconds), defaults to current time.
    
     @param options Optional parameter object
    */
    File(Object options = {});

    /*!@brief Filename, read-only property, returns the name of the file.
    
     This property is used to identify the file, usually used for display, upload or saving files.
     */
    readonly String name;

    /*!@brief Last modified timestamp, read-only property, returns the last modified time of the file (milliseconds).
    
     This property represents the last modified time of the file, in milliseconds since 1970-01-01 00:00:00 UTC.
     */
    readonly Number lastModified;
};